# Keep the Docker build context small (the Dockerfile does `COPY . .`).
# Without this, the 4+ GB `target/` and the full `.git` history are sent to the
# daemon and copied into the builder layer — slow builds, wasted disk, and on a
# managed build (Northflank) wasted build minutes/space.

# Rust build artifacts — rebuilt inside the image; never ship the host's.
target/

# Git metadata — not needed to build the binary.
.git/
.github/

# Local editor / OS cruft.
.DS_Store
*.swp

# Docs / deploy / non-build assets (the binary build needs none of these).
docs/
deploy/
conformance/

# Claude / tooling local state.
.claude/
